WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.010
1633.

2
00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:07.470
Galileo is put on trial, after a
book defending a sun-centred cosmos.

3
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.910
Church authorities read the Bible's words,

4
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.900
the sun stood still, as
a fact about astronomy.

5
00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:15.490
1859.

6
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:20.700
Charles Darwin argues that species
change slowly over vast ages.

7
00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:22.400
1927.

8
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:26.000
A Belgian physicist and Catholic
priest, Georges Lemaître,

9
00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:28.930
proposes an expanding universe.

10
00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:34.570
So did each discovery push God out, or
change how Christians read the Bible?

11
00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:38.190
In this mission, you'll follow the
arguments each discovery sparked,

12
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.180
from Rome to Oxford.

13
00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:43.940
Then you'll test an idea
called the God of the gaps.

14
00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:48.770
Your mission: find out what each discovery
really changed for Christian belief.
